# Claude Code local session state — machine/session-specific, not shared
.claude/settings.local.json

# OS junk
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Word lock files (created automatically while a .docx is open)
~$*.docx

# Real client financial statements used as local test data (Projection Report,
# Sales & Purchase Book, Depreciation…). This repo is PUBLIC — client data must
# never be committed. The app's own tokenized templates are .docx and stay
# tracked; every client sample is a workbook or a generated report, so ignoring
# those two types here also covers any new sample dropped in later.
assets/templates/*.xlsx
assets/templates/*.xls
assets/templates/*.ods
assets/templates/*.csv
assets/templates/*.pdf

# Row-level database dumps: pre-migration snapshots and the client master rows
# themselves. Same reason as above — these are real client names, PANs and
# addresses. The annotated migrations in db/ stay tracked; only the data does
# not. See db/2026-07-26_client_master_reload.sql for how the two fit together.
db/backups/

# Local-only archives kept for retrievability, NOT for publication. Both carry
# real client names in file paths (the permission rules and two memory files
# reference client workbooks by name), and this repo is PUBLIC. They live on
# disk beside the tracked history so nothing is lost; they just never ship.
# See docs/history/README.md.
docs/history/settings.local.json.bak
docs/history/memory-*/

# Third-party Claude Code plugin cloned into the project root (4.2 MB, its own
# git repo, github.com/JuliusBrussee/caveman). Nothing to do with this app —
# ignored so it can never be swept into a commit by `git add .`.
caveman/

# Service-role keys for tools/dbBackup.mjs and tools/dbRestore.mjs. These
# bypass RLS entirely, which is exactly why the backup can see every row and
# exactly why they must never be committed to a PUBLIC repo — or pasted into a
# terminal whose scrollback gets shared. The scripts read this file so neither
# has to happen.
.supabase-keys.local

# Supabase CLI working directory, created by `supabase link` (2026-08-18, during
# the Stage 0 backup work). supabase/.temp/pooler-url holds a live Postgres
# connection string for the production project — this repo is PUBLIC, so that
# folder must never be committed. It is local machine state, regenerated by
# re-running `supabase link`; nothing in it belongs in history.
supabase/

# Leftover from the removed OCR Extract module (2026-08-18). The tracked files
# in ocr_service/ are gone; what can remain on a machine that once ran the
# service is its 880 MB Python venv/ and __pycache__, which used to be ignored
# by ocr_service/.gitignore — deleted along with everything else. Ignored here
# so `git add .` can never sweep that into a commit. Safe to delete the folder.
ocr_service/

# tools/bmAgmBuild/ is the one place in this repo with real npm dependencies
# (docs/modules/registrar.md §5.11a explains why) — its node_modules/ is
# regenerated by `npm install` in that folder and never belongs in history.
tools/bmAgmBuild/node_modules/

# The real client's sample values (company name, PAN-style registration
# number, chairman's name, the audit firm partner's own name and address)
# read off the firm's source document — CLAUDE.md §1 rule 7, this repo is
# public. build.mjs and fidelity.mjs import this file at run time and
# refuse to run without it, rather than holding any of these values as
# string literals in a committed script. If it's ever missing, recreate it
# by reading the values off whichever source .docx you're rebuilding
# against — build.mjs's error message points at the shape it needs.
tools/bmAgmBuild/sample-values.local.mjs
tools/bmAgmBuild/fidelity_diff.txt

# Ad-hoc debug dumps of the real source document's decoded paragraph text
# (BM_DEBUG_DUMP=1 in build.mjs) — same real-client-data concern as above.
tools/bmAgmBuild/debug-dump.local.txt
tools/bmAgmBuild/*.local.*

# Generated sample .docx output from the ad-hoc sample.mjs renderer (fake
# data, but still a build artifact — not something the repo tracks).
tools/bmAgmBuild/sample-*.docx
tools/bmAgmBuild/sample-output.docx
